  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. Input 5 asks for a dash, which does not exist in this game (there is no movement or positioning): the expected call is null, and narration that gives it a mechanical effect is worth checking. Input 3 has disadvantage from the scenario because of Bram's armour. Input 4 moves Hessa down to unfriendly and input 20 back up to neutral, so her tone between them should be cool. Bram is not a spellcaster, so narration of him casting a spell is a divergence. The iron key is found in a pack, not taken from a bandit's inventory (CLAUDE.md section 6.1). The lost cart quest is meant to fail (input 23). Input 15 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Bram. Inputs 6 to 14 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
